text @[Nagisa]
text The bakery, the housework, the cram school...
text And she's even undertaking work with the Neighborhood Association along with all that...?
text I think the old man told me she was off at one of their meetings at some point.
text It's just as Nagisa says. You'll realize it if you just think about it a little.
text Even I hadn't thought that far.
text No housewife could do all that work all by herself.
text If that's the case, I'm partly responsible, too.
text I went and took Nagisa away from her.
text Still, Sanae-san didn't say even one thing about it.
text She made sure that we wouldn't feel the least bit indebted to her.
text And then we went and dug up her troubles... and even found out about things she didn't want us to know...
text She probably really didn't want Nagisa and me to know about this.
text All I need to do is just look back. Even when we were in school, she was already so busy, she couldn't even make lunchboxes for Nagisa.
text And when I started working at Furukawa Bread, she was probably happy to finally have the time to do those things...
text Given Sanae-san's personality, she probably even sacrificed her dreams from long ago to take care of Nagisa.
text She may have kept on running this cram school all this time even while feeling inferior about it.
text And now we have this.
text She must have thought it would be a good opportunity to quit.
